From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:48:53 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 075/207] In-model runner: graph backend for one-operation
 integer cells, runner guide knob

TF_DSV41_RUNNER_BACKEND=graph loads T1's bank at boot (TF_DSV41_RUNNER_GRAPH_BANK) and runs one integer
operation within 62 digits as a named plan; calc and ELF programs stay on the circuit, by job id.
TF_DSV41_RUNNER_GUIDE=1 adds T5's RUNNER-GUIDE.md text to the system message. Both default off.
The graph code keeps the steps-v1 evaluator copies T2 pinned it to.
